.TH "BASH\-SERVER" "1" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server commands"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
bash\-server [OPTIONS]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]bash\-server\f[R] is a persistent daemon that embeds the GNU Bash
5.1 interpreter and exposes it over a Unix domain socket (or alternative
transports) for authenticated remote evaluation of shell commands.
.PP
The server links against \f[B]cygbash\-5.1.dll\f[R], providing a full
Bash environment with readline, history, job control, and all standard
builtins.
Each connected client session maintains independent shell state
(variables, functions, working directory).
Command execution is fork\-per\-command with pipe\-captured stdout and
stderr.
.PP
On startup the server generates a cryptographically random 256\-bit
authentication token, writes it to \f[I]<socket\-path>.token\f[R] (mode
0600), and begins accepting connections.
Clients must present this token via the AUTH command before any other
operations are permitted.
.PP
\f[B]bash\-server\f[R] supports three wire protocol versions.
The protocol is auto\-detected from the first byte received on each
connection:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]v1\f[R] \(en Line\-oriented text protocol (LF\-terminated).
Simple and human\-readable.
Commands: AUTH, EVAL, PING, QUIT.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]v2 (binary)\f[R] \(en Length\-prefixed JSON frames with a 6\-byte
binary header.
Supports multiplexed channels.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]v2 (NDJSON)\f[R] \(en Newline\-delimited JSON.
Same semantics as binary v2 but without the binary framing.
.PP
Auto\-detection rule: if the first byte is \f[CR]{\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(rsn\f[R], the connection uses NDJSON framing; if the first byte
has its high bit set or is in the range 0\(en5, binary v2 framing is
assumed; otherwise the connection uses v1 text protocol.
.PP
